ops at the first block, saying why; it never pushes.\ndfd2e68 docs: the plan marks e08s01 landed\nce1935b docs: the story e08s01 is landed and its dossier recorded\n6298ca3 feat: the review answers to the keys the user set for Pi's actions, closes on ctrl+c and q, names the active keys in its help, and keeps its header and help line on screen in Pi's fullscreen mode\n76cc2ad docs: the story e08s02 promises a change read beside the tree, drawn by Pi in the active theme, without pix-pretty and jiti\nfabe475 docs: the story e08s01 promises a review that answers to the keys the user set in Pi and a help that names them\na7f09e3 docs: the review surface is assembled from pi-tui components and draws a change as Pi draws its edit tool's, presentation may import pi-tui alone, and the registry records the reload key that does nothing\n8bcf50d docs: the README demonstration shows a change on a vitest project with coverage and mutation under Pi 1.0.4, the agent context gauge, and the plain-language status and report\n00cce28 docs: the plan marks the epic of the terminal showing the agents' work landed","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cee86611-8e13-46e8-8dab-36167ae356da","uuid":"186d353f-6afb-4c18-a0e8-7c4464806a8e","timestamp":"2026-10-06T18:30:44.390Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"168:## Git and commits\n169-\n170-One branch per story or per fix cycle. Commit message: `<type>: <description>`, one line, in English,\n171-whatever the language of the session or of the file changed; the types are `feat`, `fix`,\n172-`refactor`, `docs`, `test`, `chore`, `perf`, `ci`. The message states the resulting behaviour, never\n173-the process that produced it: no work-package reference, no review round, no attribution, no\n174-`Co-Authored-By`. Nothing is pushed by an automaton; `gh` for every GitHub operation, never the API\n175-directly; no issue is created by an automaton.\n176-\n177-## What is written by hand, and what is observed\n178-\n179-By hand: a produ